WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.455
Week seven.

00:00:01.505 --> 00:00:06.072
Strategy in a creative agency, with Tim Collier from Cummins and Partners.

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:07.543
The planner sits in the middle.

00:00:07.593 --> 00:00:10.155
The client has a business problem.

00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:12.633
Strategy asks how it affects the audience.

00:00:12.683 --> 00:00:15.267
Creative makes something people remember.

00:00:15.867 --> 00:00:16.667
A client hands you a five page brief with everything in it.

00:00:16.581 --> 00:00:20.560
Your first job is subtraction:

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:23.411
get it down to one line a creative team can use.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.327
To discover, use the five C's.

00:00:26.377 --> 00:00:30.752
Company, culture, category, connections, and consumer.

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:34.007
Frame it with get, who, to, by.

00:00:34.057 --> 00:00:38.623
And remember, the single minded proposition is an invitation, not a claim.

00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:44.172
The strategist's four steps: discover, synthesise, plan, instruct.

00:00:44.222 --> 00:00:47.569
And the Effie is the award that proves the work drove profit.

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:49.244
His advice?

00:00:49.294 --> 00:00:51.521
Be curious, and be opinionated.

00:00:51.571 --> 00:00:53.117
The world changes a lot.

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:54.535
People don't.
